        "id": 1281040
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-04T01:03:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Having just empty functions here tells me that the API for these functions\nare optional, so maybe this interface should be thought through a bit more.\nThey all seem to be related to events, and so could be plumbed in using the\nstandard event notification. That way, if CONFIG_AP_PWRSEQ_S0IX_ERROR_RECOVERY is set, then the event callback can be registered, and the main part of the code is untouched.\n\nThere are also calls like ap_power_sleep_set_notify, which seem to me to be a parallel notification API, so I\u0027m getting confused about the structure of all these sleep handlers, and what they do.\n\nThere should be enough of the ap_power events to be able to plumb in the appropriate code without having to insert special calls in (like these sleep calls).\nThat way, the error recovery code can be a completely separate file without any explicit calls to it, but catching everything through the standard notification API.\n\nIt may take a little thought and refactoring to get this API right, so I don\u0027t mind if this get submitted as is, if it is urgent, and then some work can be done to re-arrange it as necessary.",
      "revId": "3180b4bde358c636e43f57756228ec15ee95bbae",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9d1fa534_52dd00ac",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/ap_pwrseq/power_host_sleep.c",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 378,
      "author": {
        "id": 1523717
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-05T00:32:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Andrew, few functions sleep_start_suspend(ctx) and sleep_complte_resume(ctx) requires data to be passed, but our current event based framework doesn\u0027t support passing additional data to the callback.\nOne way is to introduce additional function parameter(void *data)to be passed to ap_power_ev_send_callbacks(event, void *data) to address this but we will loss the functionality of passing multiple events in single function call or other way is to pass (struct ap_power_ev_data data) to ap_power_ev_send_callbacks in all calling places. whats your suggestion ?",
      "parentUuid": "bfabcedc_0ee1c3c3",
      "revId": "3180b4bde358c636e43f57756228ec15ee95bbae",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d2b5e1c5_d0f83b38",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/ap_pwrseq/power_host_sleep.c",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 378,
      "author": {
        "id": 1281040
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-05T00:51:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The only arguments I see being passed as the context, which comes from host_command_host_sleep_event and only contains a counter and timeout value.\n\nThe only reason I see that this is required to be passed is if host_command_host_sleep_event gets invoked multiple times in parallel, and not sure\nif that will ever be the case.\nThis could be handled locally as a static singleton within the same file.\nThe counter is just copied from a static anyway, so that can be referenced directly. The timeout could also be a static.\n\nSometimes the original reasons for these contexts get lost, and it\u0027s only when we look at it in detail that we realise that the context is likely unnecessary as an argument, but can be better handled as a local singleton in a single module.\n\nAs I mentioned before, I don\u0027t want to hold this up in order to get a larger refactor done. But it would be good to get a clearer understanding of how these different modules/APIs interact so that they can be sensibly refactored.",
      "parentUuid": "9d1fa534_52dd00ac",
      "revId": "3180b4bde358c636e43f57756228ec15ee95bbae",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4419b085_518f53a5",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/ap_pwrseq/power_host_sleep.c",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 378,
