        "id": 1523717
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-06T01:30:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Updated the changes for handling error recovery using event based approach.\n\nhandling ap_power_sleep_notify_transition() in same s0ix error recovery events are not straight forward because ap_power_sleep_notify_transition(AP_POWER_SLEEP_RESUME) is handled in SYS_POWER_STATE_S0 instead of SYS_POWER_STATE_S0ixS0 because of below special handing.\n\n////////////////////////////////////\n /*\n                         * SLP_S0 may assert in system idle scenario without a\n                         * kernel freeze call. This may cause interrupt storm\n                         * since there is no freeze/unfreeze of threads/process\n                         * in the idle scenario. Ignore the SLP_S0 assertions in\n                         * idle scenario by checking the host sleep state.\n                         */\n                } else if (ap_power_sleep_get_notify() \u003d\u003d\n                                   AP_POWER_SLEEP_SUSPEND \u0026\u0026\n                           power_signals_on(IN_PCH_SLP_S0)) {\n                        return SYS_POWER_STATE_S0S0ix;\n                } else if (ap_power_sleep_get_notify() \u003d\u003d\n                           AP_POWER_SLEEP_RESUME) {\n                        ap_power_sleep_notify_transition(AP_POWER_SLEEP_RESUME);\n\n\n//////////////////////////////\n\nWe can consider refactoring ap_power_sleep_notify_transition related stuff as a separate task.",
      "parentUuid": "d2b5e1c5_d0f83b38",
      "revId": "3180b4bde358c636e43f57756228ec15ee95bbae",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
